From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vadik likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:15:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvgpu: Honor GA10B IOMMU bypass in guests

GA10B reaches system memory over NVLink and explicitly bypasses the Tegra
SMMU.  On bare metal the GPU has no IOMMU firmware specifier, so nvgpu uses
physical scatterlists.  A virtual IOMMU in a passthrough guest makes
nvgpu_iommuable() true, however, and causes GPU PTEs and the syncpoint aperture
to contain IOVAs that the NVLink path sends untranslated to the memory
controller.

Set the bypass and physical-scatterlist flags before the platform probe maps
the syncpoint resource, retain them when GA10B initializes its characteristics,
and do not create an IOMMU mapping for syncpoint MMIO on a bypassing GPU.  The
Orin GPUVM provides its GPU memory and syncpoint apertures as identity-backed
guest physical resources.

Signed-off-by: vadik likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
---
 nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/hal/init/hal_ga10b.c      | 5 +++++
 nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/nvhost_common.c | 2 +-
 .../gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/platform_ga10b_tegra.c     | 7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/hal/init/hal_ga10b.c b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/hal/init/hal_ga10b.c
--- a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/hal/init/hal_ga10b.c
+++ b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/hal/init/hal_ga10b.c
@@ -2066,6 +2066,11 @@ int ga10b_init_hal(struct gk20a *g)
 	 * memory.
 	 */
 	nvgpu_set_enabled(g, NVGPU_MM_BYPASSES_IOMMU, true);
+	/*
+	 * A guest may still expose an IOMMU domain for device assignment.  The
+	 * NVLink memory path cannot consume those DMA addresses.
+	 */
+	nvgpu_set_enabled(g, NVGPU_MM_USE_PHYSICAL_SG, true);
 
 	/*
 	 * ecc scrub init can get called before
diff --git a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/nvhost_common.c b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/nvhost_common.c
--- a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/nvhost_common.c
+++ b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/nvhost_common.c
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ int nvgpu_nvhost_syncpt_init(struct gk20a *g)
	 * The resulting IOVA is used to create nvgpu_mem for the syncpoint
	 * mappings later in GPU initialization.
 	 */
-	if (nvgpu_iommuable(g) && !nvgpu_is_enabled(g, NVGPU_SUPPORT_NVLINK)) {
+	if (nvgpu_iommuable(g) && !nvgpu_is_enabled(g, NVGPU_MM_BYPASSES_IOMMU)) {
 		struct device *dev = dev_from_gk20a(g);
		dma_addr_t iova;

diff --git a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/platform_ga10b_tegra.c b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/platform_ga10b_tegra.c
--- a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/platform_ga10b_tegra.c
+++ b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/platform_ga10b_tegra.c
@@ -277,6 +277,13 @@ static int ga10b_tegra_probe(struct device *dev)
 #ifdef CONFIG_OF
 	struct device_node *of_chosen;
 #endif
+	/*
+	 * Syncpoint setup runs before GPU characteristics are initialized.  Set
+	 * GA10B's NVLink memory-path flags now so syncpoint setup does not create
+	 * an IOMMU IOVA.
+	 */
+	nvgpu_set_enabled(g, NVGPU_MM_BYPASSES_IOMMU, true);
+	nvgpu_set_enabled(g, NVGPU_MM_USE_PHYSICAL_SG, true);
 
 	err = nvgpu_nvhost_syncpt_init(platform->g);
 	if (err) {
-- 
